findings.recommendation:
Add a complementary negative-direction test:
```
it('does not emit when the input is cleared but modelValue is already empty', async () => {
  // Guards against a regression that drops the `props.modelValue !== ''` clause
  // in the inputValue setter — would cause redundant '' emits on every keystroke
  // in an already-empty field.
  const wrapper = await mountSuspended(TimezonePicker, {
    props: { modelValue: '' },
  })
  const input = wrapper.find('[data-test="timezone-picker-input"]')
  await input.trigger('focus')
  await input.setValue('')
  await settle()
  // Either no emit at all, or no '' emit beyond what was already there.
  const emitted = wrapper.emitted('update:modelValue') as string[][] | undefined
  expect(emitted).toBeUndefined()
})
```
This exactly addresses the question raised in the review brief: 'if props.modelValue is already "", no emit should fire — is this tested?' — currently no.
